			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1435412">
									

<p>I like this too. It's suitably strange and sort of creepy, but more creative and thoughtful than just going straight to trying to make the hardest shudder possible run up your spine. The idea of it sitting in its cell &quot;braiding&quot; gives it unique mannerisms in line with what an animal might do when distressed or bored. It's both inhumanly strange but also rather endearing.</p>
<p>I'm sort of curious about one thing. Did the guard sock the emotional doctor in the jaw because &quot;Hey, this jerk is grabbing my flame thrower&quot;, because &quot;Whoa, this guy's going nuts&quot;, or because &quot;Hey, leave SCP-337 alone!&quot;? Not sure if that could be incorporated into the article or even should, but even if it's not I'd be curious as to how the original writer was thinking of it when they wrote it.</p>

							</div>

								
					
